      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] ❌ **Changes Requested — Please split this CL and add tests**\n\n### Review Summary\n\n*   **Functionality:** Found a silent failure masking issue in `convert_rts_snr_init_error_code`, where it maps unmapped initialization errors to `0` (success). See inline comments.\n*   **Architecture \u0026 Component Fit:** The driver correctly encapsulates sensor interactions and maps to standard Cros EC fingerprint APIs.\n*   **Code Simplicity:** The driver implementation is generally straightforward and makes good use of guard clauses.\n*   **Idiomaticity \u0026 Readability:** Global namespace pollution was identified. The private conversion functions (`convert_fp_capture_type_to_rts_capture_type`, `convert_rts_get_image_error_code`, `convert_rts_snr_init_error_code`) are missing `static` modifiers and are currently exported. \n*   **Security:** No obvious memory or resource leaks. GPIO callbacks and device config macros are safely structured.\n*   **Testing \u0026 Test Coverage:** Missing automated test coverage. A driver of this size must include unit tests using standard fakes/mocks, following the established conventions seen in `zephyr/test/fingerprint/drivers/`. Manual testing (`TEST\u003dNone`) is not an acceptable substitute.\n*   **CL Size \u0026 Scope:** Size: L (+977, -1). This CL is too large and bundles multiple logical additions together. It must be split to ensure smaller, reviewable changes.\n    *   **CL 1:** Device tree bindings (`realtek,rts5817maa.yaml`), Kconfig entries, and build files.\n    *   **CL 2:** Core sensor driver (`fingerprint_rts5817maa.c`) along with its unit tests in `zephyr/test/fingerprint/drivers/rts5817maa/`.\n    *   **CL 3:** Board integrations and shim updates (e.g. `fpsensor.c`, `realtekfp.dts`).\n*   **Commit Message:** The `BUG\u003d` tag format is incorrect (missing the Buganizer `b:` prefix) and `TEST\u003dNone` needs to be updated with automated test commands once they are added.\n\n[🔗](http:/